From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] t20: treat DS1 as the full-resolution frame channel

The T20 SDK has no FR channel: TX_ISP_EXIST_FR_CHANNEL is 0 and
TX_ISP_EXIST_DS2_CHANNEL is 1, with DS1 (index 1) the full-resolution
output and DS2 (index 2) the scaler output.

frame_channel_vidioc_s_fmt_vid_cap() still used "index != 0" as the
scaler test inherited from the T10 layout.  On T20 that sends the main
DS1 1920x1080 S_FMT through SET_SCALER, which fails; OpenIMP then reports
"IMP_FrameSource_EnableChn: set format failed" and timps never gets a
frame.

Only route the DS2 channel through the scaler bridge.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/driver/t20/sdk/source/tx-isp-frame-channel.c
+++ b/driver/t20/sdk/source/tx-isp-frame-channel.c
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@
 #include <media/v4l2-fh.h>
 
 #include "tx-isp-frame-channel.h"
+#include "apical-isp/tx-isp-core.h"
 #include "tx-isp-videobuf.h"
 #include "tx-isp-debug.h"
 #include "tx_isp/tx_isp_guard.h"
@@ -427,7 +428,13 @@
 	 * V4L2 applications reasonably expect S_FMT to be sufficient, so bridge
 	 * the requested DS dimensions into that already-proven scaler operation
 	 * before the core verifies the output geometry. */
-	if (vdev->index != 0 &&
+	/*
+	 * T20 has no FR channel: DS1 (index 1) is the full-resolution main
+	 * channel and DS2 (index 2) is the scaled sub-stream.  The old
+	 * "index != 0" test treated DS1 as a scaler channel, so the main
+	 * 1920x1080 S_FMT went through SET_SCALER and failed.
+	 */
+	if (vdev->index != ISP_DS1_VIDEO_CHANNEL &&
 	    (f->fmt.pix.width != attr->output.fmt.pix.width ||
 	     f->fmt.pix.height != attr->output.fmt.pix.height)) {
 		if (f->fmt.pix.width < attr->min_width ||
